  "title": "Unfinished Parts",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "company": "Tesla",
  "premium": false,
  "question": "Tesla is investigating production bottlenecks and they need your help to extract the relevant data. Write a query to determine which parts have begun the assembly process but are not yet finished.\n\nAssumptions:\n\nThis question is straightforward, so let's approach it with simplicity in both thinking and solution.\n\n*Effective April 11th 2023, the problem statement and assumptions were updated to enhance clarity.*",
  "notes": [
    "parts_assembly table contains all parts currently in production, each at varying stages of the assembly process.",
    "An unfinished part is one that lacks a finish_date.",
    "The bumpers in step 3 and 4 are the only item that remains unfinished as it lacks a recorded finish date.",
    "The dataset you are querying against may have different input & output - this is just an example!"
  ],
  "tables": [
    {
      "table_name": "parts_assembly",
      "columns": [
        {
          "column_name": "part",
          "data_type": "VARCHAR(255)"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "finish_date",
          "data_type": "DATETIME"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "assembly_step",
          "data_type": "INT"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sample_data": {
    "parts_assembly": [
      {
        "part": "battery",
        "finish_date": "01/22/2022 00:00:00",
        "assembly_step": "1"
      },
      {
        "part": "battery",
        "finish_date": "02/22/2022 00:00:00",
        "assembly_step": "2"
      },
      {
        "part": "battery",
        "finish_date": "03/22/2022 00:00:00",
        "assembly_step": "3"
      },
      {
        "part": "bumper",
